Subject: [PATCH] ktls: allow server-side RX splice

Expose the receive socket to the splice path whenever kernel RX is
enabled, including connections accepted by a TLS server.

Remove the server-role guard and its warning so the kTLS RX splice path
can be tested with a TLS-terminating proxy. Keep the kernelRx check and
existing handling of non-application-data records and read errors.

This removes the restriction for testing; it does not address the
unspecified failure cited by the old warning.

Based on sing-box v1.14.3.

--- a/common/ktls/ktls.go
+++ b/common/ktls/ktls.go
@@ -94,10 +94,6 @@ func (c *Conn) SyscallConnForRead() syscall.RawConn {
 	if !c.kernelRx {
 		return nil
 	}
-	if !*c.rawConn.IsClient {
-		c.logger.WarnContext(c.ctx, "ktls: RX splice is unavailable on the server size, since it will cause an unknown failure")
-		return nil
-	}
 	c.logger.DebugContext(c.ctx, "ktls: RX splice requested")
 	return c.rawSyscallConn
 }
